   243	
   244	## 4. Semantics
   245	
   246	### State machine per slot
   247	
   248	Use the compact future-mask state in `R:engine_rs/src/myolie_sampler.rs:113–265`. Let `u` be completed units, `p` submitted market orders, `h` submitted HIREs before the frame, `A=actors`, `O=order_limit`, `H=hire_limit`, `ready=(u==A)`. All slots first reject negative/out-of-width tokens. All transitions below occur only after admission. `δ0` means singleton zero; state does not retain item/digit values after their support effect ends (the input frame retains them for rendering).
   249	
   250	| Slot | `allows` after vocabulary bounds | `advance` |
   251	|---|---|---|
   252	| 0 `unit_actor` | `{u}` until ready, else `{0}` | No semantic change; next slot. |
   253	| 1 `unit_kind` | `1..18` until ready, else `{0}` | 0→None; 6/7→Transfer; 8→Plant; other admitted kinds→Ordinary. |
   254	| 2 `unit_target` | `{0}` always | No semantic change. Width 128 is reserved, not spatial targeting. |
   255	| 3 `unit_item` | Transfer: `1..12`; Plant: `1..5`; otherwise `{0}` | Plant becomes Ordinary after validating its item. |
   256	| 4 `unit_quantity_present` | Transfer: `{0,1}`; otherwise `{0}` | Save present; absent Transfer becomes Ordinary. |
   257	| 5 `unit_quantity_high` | Present: `0..31`; otherwise `{0}` | `quantity_high_zero = present && token==0`. |
   258	| 6 `unit_quantity` | Absent: `{0}`; present/high=0: `1..31`; present/high>0: `0..31` | Clear quantity flags; Transfer becomes Ordinary. |
   259	| 7 `market_kind` | If ready, unit None and `p<O`: `0..7`, removing HIRE unless `A+h<H`; otherwise `{0}` | 0→None, 1→Hire, 3→Seed, 4→Product, 5→Animal, 6→Sell, 2/7→Other. |
   260	| 8 `market_item` | Seed: `1..5`; Product: `{1,9}`; Animal: `10..12`; Sell: `1..9`; otherwise `{0}` | Product/Animal/Sell become Seed, a shared quantity-bearing phase. |
   261	| 9 `market_quantity_high` | Seed: `0..31`; otherwise `{0}` | No semantic change. |
   262	| 10 `market_quantity` | Seed: `0..31`; otherwise `{0}` | Seed becomes Other. |
   263	| 11 `stop` | `{1}` iff ready, unit None and market None; otherwise `{0}` | 1→terminal `None`; 0→new frame with `u += unit!=None`, `p += market!=None`, `h += market==Hire`; reset slot and local flags/phases. |
   264	
   265	The support-only phase `Seed` after market item does **not** change the decoded kind: use the original typed frame's kind for its command. Sources: `R:engine_rs/src/myolie_sampler.rs:147–258`; H:43–52. This detail prevents incorrectly forcing quantities for only BUY_SEED while masking BUY_PRODUCT/BUY_ANIMAL/SELL.
   266	
   267	### HIRE, STOP, NONE and EMPTY
   268	
   269	The exact inequality is **`A + exclusive_prefix_submitted_HIREs(p) < H`** at an available market slot, with default `H=241`. The increment happens at the end of the admitted HIRE frame, even if the kernel later cannot afford it. No cash, forecast, opponent identity or execution outcome enters grammar state. Inductively, after an admitted HIRE `A+h <= H <= 241`; if `A==241`, no HIRE is admitted. When `H<A`, zero HIREs are admitted although the existing actor count remains valid. Thus grammar-admitted HIREs cannot turn 241 actors into 242. The kernel performs at most one hire per HIRE order and then clears that order (`W:engine_rs/src/lib.rs:4004–4022`); day reset may reduce actors, which does not invalidate the bound. Sources: `W:docs/kaggriculture-contract.md:212`; `R:engine_rs/src/myolie_sampler.rs:176–181,250–258`.
   270	
   271	All A actors get a unit frame in ordinal order, including PASS. Market positions start at frame A. The **first final NONE** is the STOP frame, after all HIRE corrections in the heads; all slots are zero except `stop=1`. At `p==O`, market kind is forced NONE, ensuring the extra sentinel after a full queue. NONE at `p<O` is a sampled early STOP, retaining its slot-7 probability; the forced sentinel has zero density. Later positions have zero density and are omitted from the active program. These density rules belong to 2.3, while Rust validates the resulting final program (H:63–83). Maximum length is `241+10+1=252`.
   272	
   273	EMPTY is market kind 7, emits **`[]`**, increments `p`, leaves HIRE count unchanged and has `stop=0`. It never shortens the queue. Structural NONE emits no JSON order. A standalone `[]` or `null` unit command is outside the canonical grammar. Sources: `W:docs/kaggriculture-contract.md:185–213`; `R:engine_rs/src/myolie_sampler.rs:349–380`.
   274	
   275	### Canonical JSON and kernel boundary
   276	
   277	**Cross-task actor-order invariant (Claude review R3).** Unit frame `i` ↔ `unit_actor = i` ↔ own `actor_slot = i` in the Task 1.3 observation ↔ engine unit index `i` (0 = farmer, `i ≥ 1` = `hands[i-1]`, the order `Game::step` iterates at `W:engine_rs/src/lib.rs:1604`). The grammar cannot check this alone; 1.3's writer must emit own actors in exactly this order, and the 1.2 kernel test in §5.6 asserts it on a multi-hand state by giving each hand a distinct movement and checking each moved to the expected cell.
   278	
   279	Return an object with keys inserted **farmer, hands, market**, farmer = unit 0, hands = units 1..A−1 in order, market = exactly the submitted non-NONE orders in order. All three keys are present, including empty arrays. Numeric quantities are JSON integers; no nulls, aliases, metadata, STOP command, actor id arguments or spatial targets.
   280	
   281	| Kind | Exact JSON command |
   282	|---|---|
   283	| Unit 1–5, 9–18 | `["PASS"]`, `["NORTH"]`, `["SOUTH"]`, `["EAST"]`, `["WEST"]`, `["WATER"]`, `["HARVEST"]`, `["DROP"]`, `["BUILD_COOP"]`, `["BUILD_PASTURE"]`, `["FEED"]`, `["FERTILIZE"]`, `["COLLECT_FERTILIZER"]`, `["CARE"]`, `["DIG"]`, respectively. |
   284	| Unit 6/7 | `["PICKUP", ITEM]` / `["PLACE", ITEM]` if absent; append integer `32*high+low` if present (1–1023 only); ITEM any action item 1–12. |
   285	| Unit 8 | `["PLANT", CROP]`, crop action items 1–5, no quantity. |
