   608	- **R1: strict canonical `encode` added (interfaces §2, tests §5.4, fixture schema, acceptance).** The plan makes the Rust grammar the single source of truth for C6, and Tasks 1.5 and 5.1 must turn recorded JSON actions into v4 tokens. With decode-only, Python would have to re-implement enums, arities and HIRE capacity. `encode` reuses the same `State` walk, fails without writing on error, uses error categories aligned with the reference codec's rejection table, and has round-trip laws checked on every accepted fixture program and replay action. Rejected replay candidates are recorded as negative encode oracles.
