kg/reference-2026-09-29:ops/cookbook-cleanup-2026-09-29/before/cookbook/references/shared-ppo-adapts-game-batches-without-a-second-loop.md:53:The initial game configs set `checkpoint_freq: 100000` to activate the retained evaluation/promotion path. This is an engineering starting cadence, not a measured optimum; evaluation game count follows `n_envs`, making the initial two-environment recipe a very small selection sample. `OWL_ALLOW_CPU_DDP=1` explicitly enables Gloo/CPU diagnostics with CPU DDP device IDs; normal multi-rank operation still requires CUDA. A two-rank CPU CLI diagnostic reportedly completed two updates/16 global game transitions after using an IPv4 rendezvous; the initial macOS standalone rendezvous failed DNS resolution. The retained full 8,294,450-parameter CPU two-rank log was independently inspected: three updates reach 96 global game transitions and 192 learner-seat turns. Neither proves GPU scaling or speed; exact commands/results belong to the final port receipt.
kg/reference-2026-09-29:ops/cookbook-cleanup-2026-09-29/before/cookbook/references/shared-ppo-adapts-game-batches-without-a-second-loop.md:105:By default the canonical runner evaluates `env.n_envs` complete games on rank0 after checkpointing; other ranks wait for the result broadcast. The inner native game loop has no per-turn progress log. At4,096 environments/rank, the first half-hour attempt completed524,288 training transitions and saved its checkpoint, but the agent interrupted the ongoing first evaluation after interpreting sparse output as a stall. The resulting traceback was KeyboardInterrupt in native `env.step`, with no observed OOM. This was an agent interruption, not a demonstrated pipeline failure. Do not infer a hang from an unchanged PPO progress counter or an idle/collective-waiting GPU during root-only evaluation. Resume preserves candidate, optimizer and incumbent under the same W&B identity; the receipt distinguishes interrupted and resumed portions.
kg/reference-2026-09-29:ops/default4096-2026-09-29/results.md:15:At4,096 env/rank, each PPO update collects524,288 global game transitions and plans2,048 optimizer steps/rank. Evaluation is rank0-only and uses4,096 full games because it inherits env.n_envs. It has no per-turn progress log; rank1 waits for a broadcast. GPU snapshots during this phase are not useful training utilization estimates. Checkpoint frequency100,000 causes evaluation after every update at this collection size.
