Commit recorder source "'`scripts/record_kaggriculture_env_reference.py`, fixed policy `scripts/kaggriculture_env_reference_policy.py`, its source test `tests/tools/test_record_kaggriculture_env_reference.py`, and a bounded Rust recorder adapter `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/1.4/reference_recorder.rs`. Recorder exports R via `git archive` into a fresh temporary directory (no `.git`, no branch/worktree modification); writes the adapter only into that exported copy as an example and uses R'"'s **actual "'`TrainingBatch`** constructor/step/output, not a new simulation loop pretending to be the oracle. Load reference actor_codec directly from the exported source for program recording. Offline missing dependencies stop recording; Claude may prepare an export'"'s dependencies outside this Mac brief task.

Exactly 16 games, seeds 17000..17015, stride=1, processed **one live game at a time**, default kernel config/719 transitions, both seats, with auto-reset captured. A deterministic observation-local fixed policy (not learned, no random draws or hidden policy state) uses current step/actor count: step 0 seat0 PASS plus ordered BUY_SEED WHEAT 2, BUY_ANIMAL GOOSE 1, BUY_PRODUCT WHEAT 3, HIRE, BUY_LAND; seat1 PASS plus BUY_PRODUCT WHEAT 2. Seat0 farmer steps 1..6: PICKUP GOOSE (omitted quantity), BUILD_COOP, PLACE GOOSE (omitted quantity), NORTH, PLANT WHEAT, WATER; step8 HARVEST deliberately too early. Seat1 sells WHEAT 2 at step2. All extant hands PASS, all other farmer turns PASS; step10 inserts EMPTY then BUY_PRODUCT WHEAT 0 before STOP. This starts at the shed-adjacent NW spawn, and NORTH stays in NW (W:engine_rs/src/lib.rs:2895–2911,3191–3258,3377). Later do not water/feed: starvation and drought occur. Record exact JSON/tokens and **assert** nonzero S,D,I, executed hires, animal placements and sales; if the prelude does not produce these, fix and re-review the policy before freezing, never relax the coverage assertion.

