## Adapter behavior and generations

`allocate_observation_buffers` writes the29 shapes/dtypes in the copied inventory and constructs **existing** `KaggricultureObsBatch` and `KaggricultureActionMask`. Build exact named NumPy views once in an internal typed `NativeArrays` holder; it mirrors binding parameters, not another policy schema. All tensor storage retained. No `.numpy()`/shape inference/reward recalculation per step; no returned NumPy allocations. Allocate six transition tensors for each generation and pass all35 keywords explicitly to1.4. Fail requested pinning if allocator unavailable; CPU tests pass pin_memory=False. Orbit behavior is unchanged.

`_Generation` owns obs, six outputs, native views, optional event, and monotonic generation identity. Constructor initializes A via native.observe. Before each mutation choose alternate, wait its outstanding event on CPU, then invoke native. On failure retain active A/B reference and all published bytes; on success switch properties and return that generation. `reset`/`truncate_envs` follow the same protocol, including copying unselected observations/unchanged transitions natively. `terminal_metrics` delegates lazily; snapshot JSON/seed tuple are diagnostics only. Do not expose a lifecycle explicit-state loader.

Action input accepts only KaggricultureActions with exact int64 CPU tensors, `[E,2,252,12]`/`[E,2]`, C-contiguous; rejects GPU/dtype/shape/strides instead of silently casting/copying. Task3.1 owns device→CPU action transfer and contiguous materialization. Native checks every grammar constraint. Truncate mask must be exact bool CPU `[E]`; no `.cpu()` surprise synchronization in adapter.

Two-generation contract: keep A unchanged when stepping B; before reuse of A wait A'"'s last event. "'`record_copy_completion(obs,device=...)` identifies the leased generation; CUDA creates/records `torch.cuda.Event` on `torch.cuda.current_stream(device)` **after all reads**, including rewards/dones/masks/transition copies. Unknown/stale batch errors explicitly. All streams must join before recording. A device wait alone is insufficient to stop native CPU writes, so adapter synchronizes the event. CPU uses no event/cuda calls. Repeated loop steps may proceed without record calls for synchronous CPU consumers, whose retained values must be copied before reuse.

Native methods cannot know whether external CUDA work was queued; the trainer'"'s required completion call is part of the API contract and tested at every copy site in3.1. No claim that A/B alone ensures DMA safety. No claim of fixing historical Task0.2 GEMM overflow.

